{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"881b80e2-f6a1-46b2-b81b-6820ce476c09","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Start with sine as a dashed reference. Its amplitude is one, and one full cycle takes two pi.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Compare two sine graphs"},{"op":"figure","id":"waves","region":"right","frame":{"x":[0,6.2831853072],"y":[-2.4,2.4],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x (radians)","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"base","y":"sin(x)","domain":[0,6.2831853072],"stroke":"dashed","label":"reference"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"reference","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"y=\\sin x:\\quad A=1,\\ T=2\\pi"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"881b80e2-f6a1-46b2-b81b-6820ce476c09","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Multiplying outside sine doubles every height. The peaks reach two, but the cycle still takes two pi.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"stretch","on":"waves","marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"twosin","y":"2*sin(x)","domain":[0,6.2831853072]},{"kind":"point","id":"peak","at":{"on":"twosin","x":1.5707963268},"label":"2 sin x"},{"kind":"segment","from":[1.5707963268,0],"to":{"at":"peak"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"measure","from":[0,-2.2],"to":[6.2831853072,-2.2],"label":"2π"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"outside","anchor":{"el":"reference","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"y=2\\sin x:\\quad A=2,\\ T=2\\pi"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"881b80e2-f6a1-46b2-b81b-6820ce476c09","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Multiplying inside sine doubles the phase speed. The amplitude stays one, while two complete cycles fit into the same interval.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"compress","on":"waves","marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"sindouble","y":"sin(2*x)","domain":[0,6.2831853072]},{"kind":"point","id":"fastpeak","at":{"on":"sindouble","x":0.7853981634},"label":"sin 2x"},{"kind":"measure","from":[0,2.2],"to":[3.1415926536,2.2],"label":"π"},{"kind":"point","at":{"on":"sindouble","x":3.1415926536}}]},{"op":"equation","id":"inside","anchor":{"el":"outside","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"y=\\sin(2x):\\quad A=1,\\ T=\\frac{2\\pi}{2}=\\pi"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Which graph has taller peaks, and which completes more cycles from 0 to 2π?","expected_gist":"2 sin x has taller peaks; sin 2x completes more cycles."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"881b80e2-f6a1-46b2-b81b-6820ce476c09","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Outside factors change amplitude; inside factors change period. At pi over two, the first graph reaches two while the second crosses zero.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"compare","on":"waves","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"fastzero","at":{"on":"sindouble","x":1.5707963268}},{"kind":"text","at":[2.15,0.25],"text":"same x, y = 0","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"inside","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"y=a\\sin(bx):\\quad A=|a|,\\ T=\\frac{2\\pi}{|b|}\\quad(b\\ne0)"}],"checkpoint":null}}
